-- The world's Dragon Stone Alchemy switch, told to a person's client (Hiob,
-- 1 October: "da sie to tez z ekwipunku wypierdolic? bo dziwnie to wyglada
-- jak jest alchemia a w grze jej nie ma").
--
-- The switch is the event flag m2_dragon_soul_off (M2_DRAGON_SOUL in .env,
-- the launcher's difficulty window; the classic panel's card sets it live):
-- every handler of dragon_soul, dragon_soul_refine and dragon_soul_shop asks
-- it, and so does the bots' pass. The Alchemy's window, though, is the
-- client's own - the button in the bag and the O key open it whatever the
-- world says. So the client is told at every entry into the game, a login or
-- a warp: "DragonSoulSwitch 1" while the Alchemy is on, "DragonSoulSwitch 0"
-- while it is off (client-root/dragonsoulswitch.py hides the button, lets O
-- and the button open nothing and closes the window). A login handler runs
-- only once the character is in the game (input_db.cpp's QuestLoad waits for
-- PHASE_GAME), so the command never meets a client still loading. A timer of
-- the person's own looks at the switch every few seconds and says it again
-- when it moved, so a change the panel makes live reaches a client in the
-- game. The same timer is dragon_soul.quest's: a timer runs the handlers of
-- every quest that has one for its name, and there it takes the Alchemist's
-- letter and arrow back when the switch goes off (watch_switch). At a login
-- or a warp nothing is left to take: the letter handlers ask the switch
-- before they send anything, and the engine drops a quest's arrows at a
-- logout.
--
-- A client that does not know the command writes it to its syserr.txt and
-- keeps the button, as before. A bot has no client: nothing here runs for it.
quest dragon_soul_switch begin
	state start begin
		-- Tell the client what the switch says: always at an entry into the
		-- game, where the client starts from nothing, and from the timer only
		-- when it moved since. "told" is what this person's client last heard,
		-- 2 for on and 1 for off, so 0 - never told - differs from both.
		function tell(always)
			local on = 1
			if game.get_event_flag("m2_dragon_soul_off") ~= 0 then
				on = 0
			end
			if always or pc.getqf("told") ~= on + 1 then
				pc.setqf("told", on + 1)
				cmdchat("DragonSoulSwitch " .. on)
			end
		end

		when login with not pc.is_playerbot() begin
			dragon_soul_switch.tell(true)
			loop_timer("dragon_soul_switch_look", 5)
		end

		when dragon_soul_switch_look.timer begin
			dragon_soul_switch.tell(false)
		end
	end
end
